# Cryptic Caves, ruling 2019-07-12: "If you control two Cryptic Caves and exactly three other lands, you can activate the last
# ability of only one of the Cryptic Caves. As soon as the cost for that ability is paid, you will no longer control enough
# lands to activate the ability of the second Cryptic Caves." Bot1 (with an Icetill Explorer for a second land play each
# turn) controls on turn 5 a Forest, two Islands and two Cryptic Caves, and an untapped Mox Pearl and Mox Jet. The first Caves is
# activated (it counts itself among the five) and draws a card; the second one is then refused (four lands, with its {1} and
# itself untapped) and nothing more is drawn: one card in hand.

[Bot1 Deck]
Icetill Explorer
Forest
Cryptic Caves
Cryptic Caves
Mox Emerald
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Icetill Explorer.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Cryptic Caves.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Cryptic Caves.Play
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Cryptic Caves.Activate(Ability: Draw)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Hand.Count = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
! Bot1.Battlefield.Cryptic Caves.Activate(Ability: Draw)
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Hand.Count = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 8
